From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 16:39:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/8] ci: add commit hooks (prek workspace), shared configs, PR
 title check, release preview, dependabot

- Commit hooks with prek in workspace mode: one `prek install` at the root runs every tool's own .pre-commit-config.yaml from inside the tool folder (unchanged, so they keep working in the old repositories) plus the root .pre-commit-config.yaml (workflows, dependabot.yml, shared configs). tools/query-tool/.pre-commit-config.yaml: its husky/lint-staged checks, its CI spelling check and the post-merge npm ci as hooks.
- shared/ and scripts/sync-shared.py: configs shared by several tools live once in shared/ and are copied into the tool folders listed in shared/files.yaml (commit hook; CI fails on a differing copy). The list starts empty.
- pr-checks.yml: conventional PR titles (action-semantic-pull-request, optional tool scope), an informational release-please dry run in the job summary, and the prek job (all hooks on all files).
- .github/dependabot.yml replaces the per-repo copies; adds grouped Docker base image updates (no major or python minor updates).
- Root pull request template.
